      "writtenOn": "2019-10-01T17:45:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I copied this from grunt, but all the implementations I looked at  (PWM or GPIO) look pretty much the same. I guess I could at least go to the trouble of supporting all the colors I went to the trouble of defining.\n\nThe description and type of |brightness| suggest that it should contain a specific brightness setting (0-255) for each \"color channel,\" but the individual LEDs (PWM channels) won\u0027t necessarily correspond to the colors in |ec_led_colors|. It would kind of make sense if there were a reasonable way to average across values of |led_color_map|, e.g. blue at brightness 198 and amber at brightness 50 means drive the blue LED at (198 / 255 * 100)%, red at (50 / 255 * 100)%, and green at (50 / 255 * 75)%. That\u0027s kind of crazy, though, and I don\u0027t see any code like that.\n\nThe existing implementations appear to take |brightness| as a one-hot encoding of which of the colors in |ec_led_colors| should be set. For the implementations I looked at, it would make more sense if |brightness| had type |enum ec_led_colors|. The only place I can find that sets these values is in ectool, and it contemplates the possibility of brightness ranges for each color. I don\u0027t see any code in the EC codebase that would actually support that, but maybe I\u0027m missing something.\n\nThoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "a7de8930_f9e1410d",
